error E0053: values of different types are combined  grades.mo:28:28

  28 |     return None if score < 0 or score > 100
     |                            ^ expected Option(Int), found Int or BigInt or Byte or Decimal or Float

Comparing or combining values of different types is an error (reference 3).

error E0050: a name isn't visible in this block  grades.mo:42:18

  42 |   return None if len(scores) == 0
     |                  ^^^ not visible in this block

The library has no len or length: a list's length is list.size, and a text's is text.char_count or text.byte_count (reference 3.4).

error E0075: arithmetic is used on a type without Number  grades.mo:76:11

  76 |     None: student.name + ": no scores"
     |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^ expected Int or BigInt or Decimal or Float, found Text

Text has no Number, so + doesn't join texts; insert them into one text instead, as in "#{a}#{b}" (reference 3.4).

error E0051: a visible name is bound again  grades.mo:84:5

  84 |     number += 1
     |     ^^^^^^ this name already has a meaning

  --> grades.mo:82:3
  82 |   number = 0
     |   ^^^^^^ the other meaning of this name

While a name is visible it can't be bound again; to assign it again, declare it with var where it is first bound (reference 6.2).

Fix: declare it with var
  grades.mo:82:3
  82 |   var number = 0

